From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:16:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 80/85] hjviewer: review fixes, applock lane

W13 app lock:
- A cancelled or failed prompt no longer turns the lock off. local_auth's
  error codes are not read any more (local_auth_darwin reports a cancel
  and a wrong Face ID or passcode as NotAvailable, Android a busy sensor);
  after any non-success the app asks isDeviceSupported() again, and only
  a device that can no longer authenticate turns the lock off (unlock) or
  lets the switch go off without a success. A failing question keeps the
  lock; no_fragment_activity no longer opens it.
- While the lock is on, a plain cover is up whenever the app is inactive
  or in the background, so the app switcher and Recents show no remote
  screen; on return it becomes the lock screen or goes.
- A background that begins during the switch's prompt counts again, after
  the chosen time plus 30 seconds; the no-count rule stays for the lock
  screen's own prompt (the Android passcode activity).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
