+/// The outcome of a prompt: `success` is authenticate()'s true; `deviceSupported` is
+/// isDeviceSupported(), asked again after anything else (and true when that question fails).
+/// authenticate()'s error codes never decide it: local_auth_darwin reports a cancel and a wrong
+/// face or passcode as 'NotAvailable' too, and Android a busy sensor, so a code would let anyone
+/// who holds the phone open the app by cancelling. Only a device that has neither biometrics nor
+/// a passcode any more is [HjvAuthOutcome.unavailable].
+HjvAuthOutcome hjvAuthOutcome(
+        {required bool success, required bool deviceSupported}) =>
+    success
+        ? HjvAuthOutcome.success
+        : deviceSupported
+            ? HjvAuthOutcome.failed
+            : HjvAuthOutcome.unavailable;
+
+/// A background that began while the switch's prompt was showing (Android shows the device
+/// passcode in another activity) counts only when it lasts this much longer than the chosen time.
+const kHjvAppLockSwitchGrace = Duration(seconds: 30);
+
+/// What covers the app: nothing, a plain screen while the app is not in the foreground (so the
+/// app switcher's picture shows no remote screen), or the lock screen that asks.
+enum HjvAppLockCover { none, shade, lock }
 
